<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer - stability pact needed to secure EMU.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer - stability pact needed to secure EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Thursday that a stability pact was necessary to stop the European monetary union from ripping apart.</p>
<p>Speaking to journalists in Bonn, Tietmeyer added that this stability pact should be as close as possible to that envisioned by German finance minister Theo Waigel.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in favour of a hard currency union and against a weak currency union. Fiscal discipline must be secured, or else the danger that the EMU could be torn apart is very high,&quot; said Tietmeyer.</p>
</text>
